//! # flux-importer
//!
//! Translates Flux bytecode into synthetic MIR that can be consumed
//! by the cuda-oxide compilation pipeline (`mir-importer` → `mir-lower` → `llvm-export` → PTX).
//!
//! ## Architecture Position
//!
//! ```text
//! Agent Intent
//!     ↓ (LLM / user / agent)
//! Flux Bytecode
//!     ↓ THIS CRATE (flux-importer)
//! Synthetic MIR (compatible with cuda-oxide mir-importer output)
//!     ↓ mir-lower
//! Pliron IR (NVVM dialect)
//!     ↓ llvm-export
//! LLVM IR → PTX
//! ```
//!
//! ## Why Flux?
//!
//! Flux bytecode is agent-native — it can be generated by LLMs, compiled from
//! higher-level DSLs, or hand-written. By inserting a Flux→MIR bridge before the
//! cuda-oxide pipeline, we enable *agents to compile their own GPU work* without
//! needing to generate Rust source code.

